  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation is on an explicitly declared function with a body, `fn[fingerprint]` in `impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Fingerprinting]`. It is a valid form for the built-in, and the commentary is fenced.\n\nThe reason is substantive and matches the source:\n- The enclosing test, `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets`, is meant to record only an outgoing-edge dependency. It asserts `Dependency::OutgoingEdges(1, (), edge_fingerprint(&graph, &[2]))`.\n- `fingerprint` is a required `Fingerprinting` trait method. Its body panics, so reaching it would show that node contents were read.\n- `edge_fingerprint` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs` hashes only sorted and deduplicated `node_path` segments. It never calls `Fingerprinting::fingerprint`, so the unexecuted `fingerprint` body is consistent with the test.\n- The sibling stubs `node_content` and `render` in the same test follow the same selection-only design.\n\nI found no gap.",
